Live-refresh fixes, empty-service fallback, floating save, searchable Company (v0.141)

Four separate asks from Dan's follow-up after v0.140:

1. Available Services page's "Refresh from live lookup" updated the
   checkbox state but not the list it's rendered from (the
   "available-services" react-query cache) - so a brand new code the sweep
   just found only actually appeared after leaving the page and coming back
   (re-fetching from scratch). AvailableServices.tsx now writes the
   refreshed list straight into that query's own cache via
   queryClient.setQueryData() on both the refresh and save mutations, so
   the rendered rows update immediately.

2. If a courier's live service lookup succeeds but genuinely returns zero
   matching services (not an exception - e.g. APC on a Republic of Ireland
   address, confirmed not a bug separately), the order screen's Service
   dropdown was left completely empty, forcing straight to free text.
   ApcShippingService.checkServiceAvailability()/
   DpdShippingService.listAvailableServices() now treat an empty-but-
   successful result the same as a failed live call: fall back to every
   known/allowed cached service, with live=false and a liveError explaining
   why ("APC/DPD returned no services for this address/weight"). The
   frontend already rendered whatever `services` came back and already
   showed `liveError` when not live, so no frontend change was needed for
   this part.

3. Save button on both Available Services pages (DPD and APC) switched
   from the old inline button at the bottom of the list to the floating
   button + SavedBadge pattern already used on Settings.tsx and the order
   screen - same fixed bottom-right placement, same "Saved." pill.

4. "Company (B2B credit account)" on the order screen is now a searchable
   type-to-filter field instead of a plain <select> - reuses the existing
   SearchableSelect component (previously only used for the company filter
   on Invoice Reports) rather than building a new one. SearchableSelect
   gained a `clearLabel` prop ("All" by default, kept for Invoice Reports;
   "None" for this field, matching the old <select>'s "None" option).

